<% content_for :title, "Transparency — Turf Monster" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "Everything that makes Turf Monster verifiable in one place: our open-source on-chain program, proof of reserves, and policies." %>

<div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-8 px-2 space-y-10">
  <header class="space-y-2">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-heading">Transparency</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary text-base leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      Everything that makes Turf Monster verifiable in one place: our open-source
      on-chain program, proof of reserves, and policies. Entry fees and prize pools
      settle on the <strong>Solana</strong> blockchain in USDC, so anyone can audit the
      numbers directly rather than trusting a custodial balance.
    </p>
  </header>

  <%# Featured: On-Chain. Tiles carry status: :reviewed for the green accent. %>
  <%= render "admin/hub_section", title: "On-Chain" do %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", status: :reviewed,
          name: "Smart Contract", url: contract_path,
          note: "On-chain program, instructions & 2-of-3 multisig auth model" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", status: :reviewed,
          name: "Proof of Reserves", url: proof_of_reserves_path,
          note: "Live on-chain balances backing the prize pools" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", status: :reviewed, external: true,
          name: "Source Code", url: "https://github.com/amcritchie/turf-vault",
          note: "Open-source Anchor program (Solana)" %>
  <% end %>

  <%# Program-ID / authority callout. Links to the contract page.

      THE PROGRAM ID BELOW IS PINNED TO MAINNET ON EVERY CLUSTER, ON PURPOSE.
      QA runs devnet, so on turf-monster-qa this line names a program QA does
      not talk to. That is deliberate; do not "fix" it to per-cluster.

      Why: this page makes claims about the LIVE product to external
      reviewers. It is the page cited in the Phantom / Blowfish de-list
      appeal. For that reader an address that changes by environment is worse
      than a constant one, so every copy of the page names the live program.
      Decided by Mr. McRitchie on 2026-09-10 (task
      transparency-pins-mainnet-program, option b).

      Do not reason from the admin card. The card in
      app/views/contract/_section_admin_state.html.erb renders the program ID
      and upgrade authority PER CLUSTER, and that is right there: its reader is
      an operator about to propose an upgrade, who needs the truth about the
      running build. This page's reader is outside the company and needs the
      live product. Same data, opposite reader, opposite answer.

      Why a literal and not a constant: a sweep for hard-coded program IDs
      will grep app source for this address, as the Squads PDA guard in
      test/integration/contract_upgrade_authority_test.rb does for its
      addresses, and that guard exempts app/services/solana/config.rb as the
      home of its literals. A constant there would hide this pin from exactly
      that sweep. Here, the sweep lands a few lines below this reason.

      Guarded by test/views/transparency_program_id_test.rb. It renders this
      page as a devnet build and as a mainnet build, requires this address
      both times, and reads the expected address from
      config/turf_vault.mainnet.idl.json, so a mainnet redeploy to a new
      address turns it red instead of leaving this pin stale.

      The Squads sentence names no address and holds on both clusters. %>
  <%= link_to contract_path, class: "card card-hover block p-5 space-y-2 group" do %>
    <div class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted">Program & Authority</div>
    <p class="text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed">
      Program ID
      <code class="font-mono text-xs break-all text-heading" data-test="transparency-program-id">DaFv83yokwTz8msP9CzJ13eazSGk15NuUTxjkfzJzxMM</code>.
      The upgrade authority is a <strong class="text-heading">Squads V4 2-of-3 multisig</strong> &mdash;
      no single key can alter or redeploy the program.
    </p>
    <span class="text-sm text-primary group-hover:underline">View the contract breakdown &rarr;</span>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "admin/hub_section", title: "Company & Legal" do %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "About", url: about_path,
          note: "Who builds Turf Monster and how it works" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Contact", url: contact_path,
          note: "Reach the team" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Terms of Service", url: terms_path,
          note: "The rules of using Turf Monster" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Privacy Policy", url: privacy_path,
          note: "What we collect and why" %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "admin/hub_section", title: "Help" do %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "How to Play", url: help_how_to_play_path,
          note: "Pick 6 matchups, stack Turf Scores" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Help Center", url: help_path,
          note: "Guides, glossary, and FAQs" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Rules", url: turf_monster_v1_path,
          note: "Scoring, payouts, and contest format" %>
    <%= render "admin/hub_tile", name: "Phantom Wallet", url: help_phantom_path,
          note: "Connecting and using a Solana wallet" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
